    "summary": "Time-varying Hurst exponent (DFA) on |returns| shows persistent behavior (mean H=0.771, 97% above 0.5). However, incorporating H_t into volatility forecasting models (HAR-H, EWMA-H, Regime-Hurst) does NOT improve over GJR-GARCH baseline in OOS (2023-2024). No statistically significant improvement (DM test). This confirms prior findings (K138, K166) that Hurst information, while describing vol dynamics, does not translate to better OOS forecasts. The DFA method gives different H values than R/S (prior work: H=0.73 via R/S), but the forecasting conclusion is consistent."
  },
